cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Protolith in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Protolith: metamorphic phase equilibria on the Holland and Powell data"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Dougalien Systems"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/dougalien/protolith"
abstract: >-
  Protolith computes the stable mineral assemblage of a rock at one temperature and pressure,
  along a P-T path, or over a T-P grid (a pseudosection), by Gibbs energy minimization on the
  Holland and Powell (2011) dataset with the metapelite solution models of White et al. (2014)
  and the igneous set of Holland, Green and Powell (2018), with a browser interface for teaching
  and research.
keywords:
  - metamorphic petrology
  - phase equilibria
  - pseudosection
  - thermodynamics
  - Gibbs energy minimization
